Introduction 
This assessment is designed to evaluate your ability to take a business idea from 
concept and visualization through UI/UX design, frontend development, and the development 
of administration portals and CMS solutions for websites (Backend development). 
The objective is to understand how effectively you can translate business 
requirements into a strong, modern, and engaging digital experience, while demonstrating 
strong technical ability to implement the solution using clean, maintainable, and well
structured code that follows recognized standards and best practices. 
This assessment scope is intentionally kept focused, allowing you to spend your time 
demonstrating your design thinking, creativity, visualization skills, technical implementation, 
and overall development quality. (NOTE: Avoid Over Engineering and Unnecessary 
Complexity) 
The Business Scenario 
You have been asked to design and develop the digital presence of a multi-brand 
motorcycle group operating in the Middle East. 
The company represents several motorcycle brands covering different market 
segments, such as: 
• Urban Mobility 
• Adventure & Touring 
• Performance 
• Premium Motorcycles 
The motorcycle group activities include motorcycle sales, customer enquiries, test 
rides, promotions, financing, service and maintenance, parts & accessories, warranty support 
and customer care. 
The organization has physical showrooms and service centers and wants to establish a 
strong digital presence where customers can discover the company, its brands, products and 
services. 
