Each motorcycle brand may have its own identity and target audience, while 
remaining part of the overall group. 
This is intentionally a high-level business brief.  We are not defining the website 
structure, content hierarchy, customer journey or visual direction for you. Making those 
decisions is part of the assessment. 
Assessment Requirements 
Public Website 
The minimum development requirement is one fully functional and responsive homepage. 
You are welcome to develop additional pages or functionality if you believe they add 
value to your concept, but this is not required. We would prefer to see one highly polished 
homepage rather than several incomplete pages. You have freedom to determine: 
• Information architecture 
• Content and sections 
• User journey 
• Navigation 
• Calls to action 
• Visual identity 
• Typography 
• Colors 
• Imagery 
• Interactions and animations 
The implemented homepage should be fully responsive, providing consistent and 
user-friendly experience across desktop and mobile devices. 
Design / Figma Prototype 
If your complete vision extends beyond what you can reasonably implement during 
the assessment, you are encouraged to present the full proposed experience in Figma; as we 
understand that four days may not be sufficient to fully develop every aspect of a strong 
digital concept. For example, you may: 
