3. Assets, References & Attribution 
You may use appropriate third-party resources such as: Stock photography, Product 
imagery, Icons, Fonts, Illustrations, Open-source UI resources, Other design assets, AI
generated assets, etc.  
However, Any third-party resources used should be clearly referenced and attributed 
where applicable. 
Please include an Attribution / References section in your submission or README 
containing the sources of external assets and design references used. 
If you redesign or reference an existing company's website, brand, products, images, 
or other materials, you must clearly identify and reference the original source. 
Your submission must also clearly state that the redesign is created solely for 
recruitment assessment and demonstration purposes and is not intended for commercial use. 
All trademarks, brand names, copyrighted materials, and other intellectual property remain 
the property of their respective owners. 
You are responsible for clearly identifying any third-party materials used in your 
submission and providing appropriate attribution where applicable. 
Please identify where AI-generated imagery or content is used. 
4. What We Are Evaluating 
The focus of this assessment is the quality of the public-facing digital experience. We 
will consider: 
UI/UX & Visualization: Creativity, visual quality, information hierarchy, usability, brand 
presentation and overall digital experience. 
Frontend Implementation: How effectively your proposed design is translated into a 
responsive and polished working website. 
Code Quality: Code organization, readability, reusability, maintainability and adherence to 
appropriate development practices. 
